{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-84039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-84039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(0)^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot take the square root of a negative number. Therefore, the equation has no real solutions.\nSo, there are no $y$-intercepts." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-84039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dfc806161bf79f9c798a21c102614b84b0600ac87941252e6879b67a9e1f8648"} {"question" "q-84039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-84039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(0,-4)"] ["math" "(0,\\pm 4)"] ["math" "(0,\\pm \\sqrt{3})"] ["math" "(0,\\sqrt{3})"] ["text" "There are no $y$-intercepts"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-84039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "There are no $y$-intercepts"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-170558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola ${x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1$ intersects the line $y=8x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-170558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=8x,$ we first replace $y$ with $8x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-\\frac{(8x)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-\\frac{64{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4{x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ -3{x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot take the square root of a negative number. Therefore, the equation has no real solutions. So, the hyperbola does not intersect the line $y=8x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-170558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dfc806161bf79f9c798a21c102614b84b0600ac87941252e6879b67a9e1f8648"} {"question" "q-170558" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-170558" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=\\pm 3"] ["math" "x=\\pm \\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "x=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}"] ["math" "x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}"] ["text" "There are no points of intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-170558" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "There are no points of intersection"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-277805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=8$ intersects the line $y=x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-277805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x,$ we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =8 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-2$ and $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-277805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dfc806161bf79f9c798a21c102614b84b0600ac87941252e6879b67a9e1f8648"} {"question" "q-277805" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-277805" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-277805" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-277805" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-278367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The $y$-intercept of the hyperbola $\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{16}-(y-2)^{2}=1$ is$\\,(${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-278367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{16}-(y-2)^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(0-4)^{2}}{16}-(y-2)^{2} & =1 \\\\ 1-(y-2)^{2} & =1 \\\\ -(y-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y-2 & =0 \\\\ y & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $(0,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-278367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dfc806161bf79f9c798a21c102614b84b0600ac87941252e6879b67a9e1f8648"} {"question" "q-278367" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-278367" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-278367" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-278367" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-278373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "From **top to bottom**, the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1$ intersects the line $x=-5$ are\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $)\\,$\nand\n$\\,($\n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}} $).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac28a0045c42d58c70b2837967c9e3935727815c45ce9ac29171c6b0ea693c77"} {"question" "q-278373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $x=-5,$ we substitute $x=-5$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(-5)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{25}{16}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1-\\frac{25}{16} \\\\ -\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =-\\frac{9}{16} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ y & =\\pm 1.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the hyperbola intersects the vertical line $x=-5$  at the points $(-5,1.5)$ and $(-5,-1.5).$" "ca